    <string name="view_source">Open source repository</string>
    <!-- O4 (docs/DRIFT-REPORT.md): the previous wording promised that the
         complete uBO source is "bundled under assets/legal/ubo/" inside the
         APK. That is true for debug builds but release APKs exclude that tree
         (843,659 B of files no runtime code reads), so the promise was false in
         the artefact users install. This wording is true in BOTH variants: it
         points at the source repository, which is where that material lives,
         and names only files that are actually packaged with the app.
         Wording is deliberately order-independent ("named on this screen"):
         in OpenSourceActivity the URL row is added AFTER the body, so a
         "shown above" phrasing would have been wrong.
         No apostrophes: Android XML requires escaping them and a missed escape
         silently truncates the string. -->
    <string name="open_source_body">ShieldTube is open source under GPL-3.0-or-later. The complete source code, including the corresponding source for the uBlock Origin scriptlets and filter lists used by this app, is in the source repository named on this screen; the pinned upstream commits are recorded in assets/lists/SOURCES.json, which ships with this app, and in docs/LICENSING.md. adblock-rust and the Brave filter lists are MPL-2.0; uBlock Origin scriptlets and lists are GPL-3.0. The GPLv3 text is shown below.</string>
    <string name="license_title">GNU General Public License v3</string>
    <string name="source_link_unavailable">Source URL is still pending; see docs/LICENSING.md</string>

